.TH GETTIMEOFDAY 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
gettimeofday \- read wall-clock time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/time.h>
.B int gettimeofday(struct timeval* value, void* zone);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes seconds and microseconds since the Epoch to value.  Pass NULL for zone;
the Linux timezone argument and struct timezone are obsolete.  This wrapper
invokes the kernel syscall directly: unlike GNU libc's implementation, a
non-NULL zone receives the kernel's timezone information.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gettimeofday (2)
